### 1. `[MethodRpc]` internals

The attribute is defined in `Reactor\Networking\Attributes\MethodRpcAttribute.cs`. It has `Id`, `SendOption` (default `Reliable`), `LocalHandling` (default `Before`), and an obsolete `SendImmediately` (removed in 2025.5.20 — all RPCs are now immediate). It registers all `[MethodRpc]`-annotated methods into `MethodRpc` instances via `CustomRpcManager.Register`:

```csharp
foreach (var method in methods)
{
    var attribute = method.GetCustomAttribute<MethodRpcAttribute>();
    if (attribute == null) continue;
    try
    {
        var customRpc = new MethodRpc(plugin, method, attribute.Id, attribute.SendOption, attribute.LocalHandling);
        PluginSingleton<ReactorPlugin>.Instance.CustomRpcManager.Register(customRpc);
    }
    catch (Exception e) { Warning($"Failed to register {method.FullDescription()}: {e}"); }
}
```

The constructor in `Reactor\Networking\Rpc\MethodRpc.cs` validates: a static method's first parameter must be an `InnerNetObject`; an instance method's declaring type must be an `InnerNetObject`. Multiple overloads support two data types.

### 2. How `StartRpcImmediately` / `FinishRpcImmediately` are called

The exact networking call is in `Reactor\Networking\Rpc\UnsafeCustomRpc.cs`, method `UnsafeSend`:

```csharp
var writer = AmongUsClient.Instance.StartRpcImmediately(
    innerNetObject.NetId,
    CustomRpcManager.CallId,       // = byte.MaxValue (255)
    SendOption,
    targetClientId);

writer.Write(Mod);                 // ModList.Write — net id or id string
writer.WritePacked(Id);            // rpc id

writer.StartMessage(0);
UnsafeWrite(writer, data);         // write payload
writer.EndMessage();

if (ackCallback != null) {
    if (SendOption != SendOption.Reliable) throw new ArgumentException("...", nameof(ackCallback));
    AckCallbacks.TryAdd(writer, ackCallback);
}

AmongUsClient.Instance.FinishRpcImmediately(writer);
```

Local handling runs `UnsafeHandle` **Before** (if `RpcLocalHandling.Before`) or **After sending** in this same method. Ack callbacks use a `ConcurrentDictionary<MessageWriter, Action>` plus a `UdpConnection.Send` Harmony prefix patch (`MessageAckPatch`).

### 3. Send/Receive networking & serialization pattern

**Send packet layout** (via `CustomRpcManager.CallId = byte.MaxValue` as the RPC call id):
`[Mod ref][PackedUInt32 rpc id][StartMessage(0)][payload payload][EndMessage]`

**Receive** is in `Reactor\Networking\Rpc\CustomRpcManager.cs`:

```csharp
public const byte CallId = byte.MaxValue;

public static bool HandleRpc(InnerNetObject innerNetObject, byte callId, MessageReader reader)
{
    if (callId == CallId)
    {
        var manager = PluginSingleton<ReactorPlugin>.Instance.CustomRpcManager;
        var customRpcs = manager._map[innerNetObject.GetType()];
        var mod = reader.ReadMod();
        var id = reader.ReadPackedUInt32();
        var customRpc = customRpcs[mod][id];
        customRpc.UnsafeHandle(innerNetObject, customRpc.UnsafeRead(reader.ReadMessage()));
        return true;
    }
    return false;
}

[HarmonyPatch]
internal static class HandleRpcPatch
{
    private static List<Type> InnerNetObjectTypes { get; } = typeof(InnerNetObject).Assembly.GetTypes()
        .Where(x => x.IsSubclassOf(typeof(InnerNetObject)) && x != typeof(LobbyBehaviour)).ToList();

    public static IEnumerable<MethodBase> TargetMethods()
    {
        return InnerNetObjectTypes.Select(x => x.GetMethod(nameof(InnerNetObject.HandleRpc), AccessTools.allDeclared)).Where(m => m != null)!;
    }

    public static bool Prefix(InnerNetObject __instance, [HarmonyArgument(0)] byte callId, [HarmonyArgument(1)] MessageReader reader)
    {
        return !HandleRpc(__instance, callId, reader);   // returns false → skip original HandleRpc
    }
}
```

So the `HandleRpc` patch is a **Harmony Prefix** applied to every `InnerNetObject` subclass's `HandleRpc`, and returns `false` to suppress the base handler whenever the reactor `CallId` (255) is matched.

